============================================================================================
PART 3 -- per-k bites: diameter range the tail floor covers vs each union-bound bar
============================================================================================
  (monotonicity never uses |E|: a k-point cluster E of primitive diameter D has
   mu_1/7(E) >= mu_1/7(AP_{D+1}); note D >= k-1 always, so the bite starts at D=k-1.)
  k=8: bar 0.6750 not met at any n -- no bite
  k=9: bar 0.5622 not met at any n -- no bite
  k=10: bar 0.4521 not met at any n -- no bite
  k=11: bar 0.3312  bite = diam 10..15   (mu(AP_n)>=bar up to n=16)
  k=12: bar 0.1993  bite = diam 11..23   (mu(AP_n)>=bar up to n=24)
  k=13: bar 0.0565  bite = diam 12..73   (mu(AP_n)>=bar up to n=74)

============================================================================================
PART 4 -- LEG-B groundwork: exact pair-decorrelation constant (verified)
============================================================================================
  LEMMA (Fourier, rigorous): for gcd(p,q)=1, intervals I,J:
    |meas{x: frac(px) in I, frac(qx) in J} - |I||J|| <= sum_{t>=1} 2/(pi^2 t^2 pq) = 1/(3pq).
  For speeds e_i, e_j with g = gcd: bound = g^2/(3 e_i e_j).
  300 random (p,q,I,J): max |err|/bound = 0.685  (<= 1 + numeric noise expected)

  COMPOSITION (the emerging 3-leg tail program for the k=13 floor):
   LEG A (this session): primitive diam <= D1  =>  mu_1/7 >= mu_1/7(AP_{D+1}) >= m_P  [PROVED]
   LEG B (residual):     primitive diam > D1   =>  decorrelation via the 1/(3pq) pair bound
                          + staggered-window Chung-Erdos (monad target 4) -- most pairs are
                          large when the diameter is large; small-pair clusters re-enter the
                          multi-scale (P,E)-recursion / peel (canon GREEN).
   LEG C (upstream):     the bounded-spread compact reduction (THM-527-D) bounds the honest
                          domain; if its S0 <= D1 the k=13 floor is CLOSED by LEG A alone.
DONE.

