Exact rationals pinning D1 (mu_1/7(AP_n) vs m_P = 14249/252252 ~ 0.0564868):
  n=72: 34819645288711/572406237683280 = 0.060830  >= m_P
  n=73: 186314370713/3127902938160     = 0.059565  >= m_P
  n=74: 12176519786/206826915295       = 0.058873  >= m_P
  n=75: 444614591352/7652595865915     = 0.058100  >= m_P
  n=76: 2314528732/40290957525         = 0.057445  >= m_P
  n=77: 3386550777203/60135183897390   = 0.056316  <  m_P   <<< first crossing
  n=78: 801470432537/14335632074610    = 0.055908  <  m_P
==> D1 = 75: every 13-element integer E with PRIMITIVE DIAMETER <= 75 has
    mu_1/7(E) >= mu_1/7(AP_{diam+1}) >= mu_1/7(AP_76) = 2314528732/40290957525 > m_P.
(mu_1/7(AP_n) is monotone decreasing in n by the SAME subset lemma: AP_n subset AP_{n+1}.)

Residual-regime probe (primitive diam > 75, structured adversaries; numeric res=30000):
  parity-interlace diam 80: 8*{0..10} u {39,41}   mu = 0.5898
  stretch diam 90: {0,2..12,17,90}                mu = 0.5908
  jittered 7*AP diam 84                           mu = 0.8455
  near-uniform diam 96 (step 8, jitter 1)         mu = 0.8301
  interlace diam 100: 10*{0..10} u {49,51}        mu = 0.5834
  random-ish primitive diam 87                    mu = 0.9689
==> the open residual (primitive diam > 75) sits empirically at mu >= ~0.58 = 10x m_P;
    the frontier D1=75 is deep inside safe territory.
